From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: babarot <b4b4r07@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:27:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add ui.toast.duration_seconds to set how long a toast stays

An in-app toast stays for a duration fixed per kind (8 seconds for
needs-attention, 5 for finished and custom, 3 for update-installed), and
no setting changes it.

ui.toast.duration_seconds sets one duration for every kind. Left unset,
each kind keeps its own duration, so nothing changes for existing
configs. 0 keeps a toast until it is clicked, and a toast without a
target pane now closes on click too, since with 0 a click is the only
way to close it. Like delay_seconds, values above 3600 are a config
error.
